/*
Skill Rack Average of N Numbers The program must accept an integer N as the input, followed by N integers. The program must print the average of the N integers rounded to two decimal places. Boundary Condition(s): 1 <= N <= 1000 Input Format: The first line contains the integer N. The next N lines contain the N integers. Output Format: The first line contains the average of the N integers rounded to two decimal places. Example Input/Output 1: Input: 5 10 20 30 40 50 Output: 30.00 Explanation: The number of integers is 5. The sum of the integers is 150 (10 + 20 + 30 + 40 + 50). Hence the average is 150 / 5 = 30.00. Example Input/Output 2: Input: 4 12 15 18 21 Output: 16.50 Max Execution Time Limit: 4000 millisecs
*/



import java.util.*;
public class Hello {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
		//Your Code Here
      Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
      int num = sc.nextInt();

      
      int sum =0;
      for(int i =0 ; i<num ; i++){
          sum+= sc.nextInt();
         
      }
      float f = (float) sum/num;
      
      System.out.printf("%.2f",f);
	}
	
}
